### GET /v1/players/{playerId}/matches — paginated match history
###
### When to use: to list the authenticated player's past matches (newest first).
### Requires Bearer token whose sub == playerId (session JWT; data-tokens at W22).
###
### How to use: run the requests below in order. Request 1 gets the first page
### plus `nextCursor`; paste that value into request 2's `?cursor=`.
###
### Expected: 200 with { "items": [...], "nextCursor": "..." | null }.
### Error cases: limit out of range/non-numeric → 400; invalid cursor → 400;
### playerId != token sub → 403.

@apiBaseUrl = http://localhost:8080

### 1. First page
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/players/p1/matches?limit=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 2. Second page (paste nextCursor from request 1)
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/players/p1/matches?limit=2&cursor=
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 3. Limit out of range — expect 400
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/players/p1/matches?limit=500
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 4. Invalid cursor — expect 400
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/players/p1/matches?cursor=!!!invalid!!!
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}

### 5. Another player's history — expect 403
GET {{apiBaseUrl}}/v1/players/p2/matches
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
